# Slice 4 WP4 — Fix Round 1 Report

## 1. Per-Item Changes

* **F1 — Refuse positional-vs-flag disagreement**:
  In [`apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L788-L798), updated `_run_migrate` to resolve both positional `vertex_path` and flag `--vertex` when both are present. If they resolve to different vertex files, it refuses with exit code 2 and a message naming both spellings (`positional vertex target '...' conflicts with --vertex '...'`). If they resolve to the same vertex, it proceeds cleanly.
* **F2 — `--vertex` becomes REQUIRED**:
  In [`apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L769-L772), set `required=True` on `--vertex` in `_run_migrate`'s `ArgumentParser`, updated the help string to remove the ambient default prose, and removed the flagless fallback arm to `<LOOPS_HOME>/.vertex`.
* **F3 — Arrival custody domain**:
  * In [`libs/custody/src/custody/signing.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/libs/custody/src/custody/signing.py#L32), defined `ARRIVAL_DOMAIN = "loops-arrival-v1"`.
  * Implemented [`arrival_signer_for`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/libs/custody/src/custody/signing.py#L159-L203) and [`arrival_verifier_for`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/libs/custody/src/custody/signing.py#L236-L268), mirroring `fact_signer_for`/`fact_verifier_for`'s key resolution and caching under the `ARRIVAL_DOMAIN`.
  * In [`apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L829), wired `_run_migrate` to `arrival_signer_for`.
  * Dissolved test-local `ARRIVAL_DOMAIN = "test-arrival-v1"` in [`libs/migrate/tests/test_sidecar.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/libs/migrate/tests/test_sidecar.py#L67) and [`libs/migrate/tests/test_transform.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/libs/migrate/tests/test_transform.py#L61) against `custody.signing.ARRIVAL_DOMAIN`.
  * Added mutual refusal and round-trip unit tests in [`libs/custody/tests/test_signing.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/libs/custody/tests/test_signing.py#L115-L175).
  * Added domain-separation pin assertions in [`apps/loops/tests/test_store_migrate.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/tests/test_store_migrate.py#L114-L140).
* **F4 — Signer guard probes capability, not existence**:
  In [`apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L832), changed the guard to `if signer is None or signer(vertex_target.stem, "0" * 64) is None:`. Probing signer capability ensures vertices with an existing `keys/` directory (e.g. `keys/bob/`) but missing the self-observer key cleanly refuse with exit code 2 before attempting migration.
* **F5 — Multi-line refusal rendering**:
  In [`apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L37-L50), updated `_refuse_store` to split `msg.splitlines()` into distinct painted `Block.text` rows composed via `join_vertical(*blocks)`, preserving structured multi-line messages on `stderr`.
* **F6 — Pyproject metadata honesty**:
  In [`apps/loops/pyproject.toml`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/pyproject.toml#L6-L18), added `"migrate"` to `project.dependencies` and `migrate = { workspace = true }` under `[tool.uv.sources]`.
* **F7 — E2E test strength**:
  In [`apps/loops/tests/test_store_migrate.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/tests/test_store_migrate.py#L107-L146), asserted that `resolve_canonical_path(vpath) == target_path` and opened the migrated store via `main([str(vpath), "store", "stats", "--json"])`, asserting `total_facts == 2`.
* **F8 — Already-migrated guard**:
  In [`apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp4/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py#L807-L824), added a CLI pre-flight check parsing `vertex_target` with `parse_vertex_file`. If `pre_ast.store` is in arrival mode or specifies an arrival file backend, `_run_migrate` refuses with exit 2 ("already on an arrival lineage; re-migration would orphan it; deliberate re-migration is a slice-6 ceremony").

